# SafarTrip Architecture Overview

## Stack

Next.js + Prisma + MySQL on Hetzner VPS (PM2 + Nginx). PWA.  
Payments: Payme (Merchant API, JSON-RPC 2.0), Click (SHOP API, 2-phase).  
Invoicing: Didox EDO.

## Domain modules

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| inventory | room types, physical units, per-date availability |
| rates | rate plans, seasonal overrides, LOS/occupancy, pricing pipeline |
| booking | reservation lifecycle + state machine |
| payment | Payme/Click adapters, idempotency, webhook dedup |
| ledger | double-entry, commissions, partner payouts, reconciliation |
| guest | profiles, CRM, booking history |
| catalog | properties, dachas/homestays, guides, taxi, attractions |
| invoice | hotel B2B invoices (tiyin), status machine; Didox emit later via outbox |
| integration | provider catalog + per-hotel connection registry (OTA/payment/local) |
| channel | OTA channel manager: room/rate mapping, ARI sync jobs, reservation inbox; adapters stubbed until OpenTravel cert |

### Hotel ops pipeline (invoice / integrations / OTA)

```
Integrations UI → integration (connect) → channel.onOtaConnected → FULL_REFRESH job
Inventory/Rates change → channel.enqueue ARI_PUSH → adapter.pushAri (outside DB tx)
OTA reservation → channel.inbox (idempotent) → booking.create (source BOOKING_COM/…)
Invoice wizard → invoice.create (tiyin) → later Didox via outbox (no HTTP in tx)
```

## Key invariants

1. A room-night is never sold twice — DB row locks in a serializable transaction + unique constraints.
2. Sum of ledger DEBIT amounts == sum of ledger CREDIT amounts, always.
3. Booking moves only along allowed state transitions.
4. Payment webhook processed twice → exactly one effect (idempotency).
5. No external call inside a DB transaction.

## Booking lifecycle

```
PENDING → HELD → PAID → CONFIRMED → CHECKED_IN → COMPLETED
Side branches: CANCELLED, REFUNDED, NO_SHOW, EXPIRED
```

## Revenue model

5% + 5% booking commission + HMS SaaS subscription for partner properties.
